flowchart TD
    start([Define product purpose]) --> concept[Describe the problem, users and desired outcome]
%% @aidflow-context concept
%% Store only the stable product rationale in `.aidflow/concept.md`: the problem,
%% intended users, desired outcome, boundaries and success measures. Do not list
%% all features here or introduce technical implementation choices.

%% Record path: `.aidflow/concept.md`.
%% Record outline: Problem; Intended users; Desired outcome; Product boundaries and non-goals; Success measures; Decisions and evidence.
%% Mutable statuses belong in the index. Example IDs and versions are placeholders.
%% For a new project's first questions, read `reference/concept-example.md` (relative to aidflow.md).
%% @end-aidflow-context
    concept --> conceptApproval{Product concept approved?}
    conceptApproval -- No: refine the problem or outcome --> concept
    conceptApproval -- Yes: save `.aidflow/concept.md` --> conceptReady([Project concept established])
%% @aidflow-context conceptApproval
%% Save the draft before requesting approval.
%% Obtain explicit human approval for the exact current file digest. Record the
%% decision evidence in `.aidflow/index.md` according to
%% `reference/approvals.md` (relative to aidflow.md). Revisit only when the product direction materially changes.
%% @end-aidflow-context

    classDef boundary fill:#0b7fae,color:#ffffff,stroke:#0b7fae
    classDef approval fill:#fff0e8,color:#633b2c,stroke:#c68162
    class start,conceptReady boundary
    class conceptApproval approval
